    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i don't want to be a director though. that sounds like so much work. i'm just tired of the effort of pretending to be a person. every time i try to find something \"new\" i just feel more hollow because it doesn't feel like it belongs to me. it's like there's just nobody home inside anymore. does that even make sense?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It makes perfect sense that you feel hollow when your life feels like a script you didn't write. You don't need to be a director; you just need to be the author of your own story, one page at a time. Take a moment to write down the things that feel most \"yours\" right now, even if they seem small, and let that list guide your next steps. You don't have to pretend to be a person; you just have to be the person you already are, and that is enough.",
